<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_PropaneLakeFauna.xml                       UtinniPatches — authored 2026-09-25
  COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1, the_propane_lakes sheet's 2 remaining ledger slugs:
  `burner-polar-ascendant-form-blue-fire-halo-as-locomotion-alm` and
  `v-wake-propane-sea-exotic-kin-propane-native-agitated-by-pum`. Full pitch text
  for both is only stored (truncated form) at those keys in
  design/Jawa/worldbuilding/review/flora_assignment_register.decisions.json; the
  fuller prose lives in design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/the_propane_lakes.md §4
  (FROZEN — amendments add detail, never change a ruling) and
  design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/rosters/the_propane_lakes.json's own `new_defs`
  entries, both re-read before authoring anything here.

  =========================================================================
  RUT_BurnerAscendant — "The Burners, ascendant" (the_propane_lakes.md §4:
  owner, "yet more powerful here and almost required"; "the apex of the Blue
  Desert's line, and the most beautiful killer on the ice"). NOT a reskin of
  a donor mod's creature — this IS a form of this mod's own RM_Krissek
  lineage (RM_BlueDesertFauna.xml, "KRISSEK — the Burner"), checked against
  cast_assignment.csv first (Krissek itself is cast to the_blue_desert only,
  no double-booking here since this is a distinct defName/PawnKind, not a
  re-cast of Krissek itself). Body/art REUSED from Krissek's own placeholder
  (vanilla Warg, Graphic_Multi) — same "recolored placeholder, no new art"
  idiom that file's own header documents — at a brighter, paler blue-white
  tint and larger drawSize to read as the apex form rather than a duplicate.
  Checked infrastructure/artpipe/{done,pending,registry.jsonl} and
  design/Jawa/ for "burner"/"ascendant" first — clean, nothing queued or
  built.

  Mechanics: rosters/the_propane_lakes.json's own new_defs entry for this row
  flags "C#: flame-halo movement VFX + detonation-on-death (shared authoring
  with the Blue Desert's Burners)" — both now real, zero NEW C# beyond two
  small additions to the shared BlueDesertLife.cs file, wired onto BOTH
  Burner forms (see that file's own 2026-09-25 header note and RM_Krissek's
  own race.deathAction, added in the same pass):
    - RM_CompEffecter_HaloAlways: the halo is LOCOMOTION here, not a sprint
      tell (§4: "not a sprint trick... it is locomotion... always in flame
      when moving") — shows at any movement, not just Jog+/combat like
      Krissek's own RM_CompEffecter_Halo.
    - RM_DeathActionWorker_BurnerBlast: "it goes, all at once, and the field
      goes with it" — wraps vanilla DeathActionWorker_BigExplosion (the
      Boomalope's own mechanism) behind the existing nativeDetonationsEnabled
      toggle.
  Colder-tolerant than Krissek (ComfyTemperatureMax lower) per the sheet's
  own measured range (median -62.2 C, coldest LAND on the planet) and larger/
  stronger stats matching "yet more powerful ... apex of the line." Lives on
  RUT_FuelSnows (the land biome, successor to RUT_Umbra per
  UMBRA_IS_A_REGION_NOT_A_BIOME_1) — wired into BOTH RUT_FuelSnows.xml and
  its live-continuity duplicate RUT_Umbra.xml (that file's own header:
  "a full behavioural duplicate... until the terminal repaint"), matching the
  discipline that file already documents for itself.
  Solitary (wildGroupSize 1, unlike Krissek's 1~3 pack) — an apex predator,
  not a pack hunter, and this keeps ecoSystemWeight sane against Krissek's
  own Blue Desert population.

  =========================================================================
  RUT_VWake — "the V-wake creature and its kin" (the_propane_lakes.md §4,
  ruled: "propane-native, agitated by pumping, attacking pawns and pipe on
  sight"; propane_gas_deep_design.md §9 build-ladder row 5: "often-but-not-
  guaranteed, visible submerged V-wake... not the lake's origin"). No donor
  fits (checked cast_assignment.csv and RUT_PropaneLake.xml's own header,
  which explicitly names this row as unbuilt: "no PawnKindDef exists for it
  yet") — a genuinely new creature, working name taken directly from the
  sheet's own term the same way RUT_Glower reused the owner's own
  capitalized name last wave.

  Lives SUBMERGED on RUT_PropaneLake (the water biome, impassable=true,
  isWaterBiome=true) via the same vanilla mechanism the Star Wars Bestiary's
  own RSW_SandoAquaMonster already uses for the Scald's own aquatic
  predator (SeaBeasts_Sando.xml): race.waterSeeker + waterCellCost 1, so the
  engine treats liquid propane as ordinary passable terrain for this race
  specifically — no new C# needed for that half either. Body: vanilla Snake
  (Core BodyDef) for the serpentine "wake" silhouette — a bite-and-strike
  layout, no limbs, matching a submerged ambush predator rather than the
  quadruped shape every other biome resident here uses.

  "Agitated by pumping" is the ONE piece of this row not built: it depends on
  CompPipeNetwork/CompPipeRupture (propane_gas_deep_design.md §9 build-ladder
  rows 1-3, 6 — RUT_GasVent, GasSaturationTracker, the pipe network itself),
  none of which exist in this repo yet (checked: zero hits for
  CompPipeNetwork/CompPipeRupture/RUT_GasVent/GasSaturationTracker). That
  whole mechanics stack is too large for this pass and is filed separately,
  PROPANE_LAKE_PIPE_MECHANICS_1. Until it lands, RUT_VWake ships with
  ordinary elevated aggression (manhunterOnDamageChance 1.0, matching
  Krissek/Sando's own precedent for "attacks on sight") standing in for the
  ruled "agitated by pump noise" trigger — the creature exists and is
  dangerous now; the specific pump-noise hook wires on top later with no
  def rework, only a new comp reading this race's own aggression state.

  Wired into RUT_PropaneLake.xml's wildAnimals at a low commonality (0.04) —
  a rare, dangerous, "often-but-not-guaranteed" sighting per the build
  ladder's own wording, not a common resident like AA_AuroraSylph/AA_Skyeel.
  Three art jobs filed (rutvwake_v1_south/east/north) — checked artpipe
  done/pending/registry.jsonl for "vwake"/"v-wake"/"wake" first, clean.
-->
<Defs>

  <!-- =================================================================
       RUT_BurnerASCENDANT — the Burners, ascendant (propane lakes)
       ================================================================= -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RUT_BurnerAscendant</defName>
    <label>burner, ascendant</label>
    <description>Bigger than any krissek and paler for it — a coat of blue-white fire that never quite goes out, because on this ice nothing moves without burning. It does not sprint into flame the way its cousins do; it simply never stops being alight. Crews who work the lake give it a wide, permanent berth. When one finally goes down, it does not fall so much as detonate, and everything nearby learns why they call it that.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>7.5</MoveSpeed>
      <Mass>85</Mass>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <MeatAmount>0</MeatAmount>
      <LeatherAmount>0</LeatherAmount>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>0</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>-100</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>-30</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <Wildness>1.0</Wildness>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>jaws</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>20</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.6</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Teeth</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>claw</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>12</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontLeftPaw</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <race>
      <body>QuadrupedAnimalWithPawsAndTail</body>
      <bloodDef>Filth_Blood</bloodDef>
      <bloodSmearDef>Filth_BloodSmear</bloodSmearDef>
      <hediffGiverSets>
        <li>OrganicStandard</li>
      </hediffGiverSets>
      <baseBodySize>1.3</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>0.9</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.35</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>CarnivoreAnimal</foodType>
      <predator>true</predator>
      <maxPreyBodySize>1.0</maxPreyBodySize>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <lifeExpectancy>5</lifeExpectancy>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>1.0</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.15</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.3</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <!-- §4d / COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1: "it does not fall so much as
           detonate" (this def's own description above): wraps vanilla
           DeathActionWorker_BigExplosion behind nativeDetonationsEnabled. -->
      <deathAction>
        <workerClass>RimMandrake.BlueDesert.RM_DeathActionWorker_BurnerBlast</workerClass>
      </deathAction>
    </race>
    <comps>
      <!-- the halo is locomotion here, not a sprint/combat tell: shows at
           ANY movement (RM_CompEffecter_HaloAlways.ShouldShowEffecter,
           BlueDesertLife.cs §4c). Reuses Krissek's own effecterDef: the VFX
           itself needs no new art, only a different trigger condition. -->
      <li Class="CompProperties_Effecter">
        <compClass>RimMandrake.BlueDesert.RM_CompEffecter_HaloAlways</compClass>
        <effecterDef>RM_KrissekHalo</effecterDef>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.BlueDesert.RM_HydrocarbonNativeExtension" />
    </modExtensions>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalFighter</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RUT_BurnerAscendant</defName>
    <label>burner, ascendant</label>
    <race>RUT_BurnerAscendant</race>
    <combatPower>170</combatPower>
    <wildGroupSize>1</wildGroupSize>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0.3</ecoSystemWeight>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Warg/Warg</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.85</drawSize>
          <color>(150,195,230)</color>
        </bodyGraphicData>
        <dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Warg/Dessicated_Warg</texPath>
          <drawSize>0.85</drawSize>
        </dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Warg/Warg</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>1.25</drawSize>
          <color>(150,195,230)</color>
        </bodyGraphicData>
        <dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Warg/Dessicated_Warg</texPath>
          <drawSize>1.25</drawSize>
        </dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Warg/Warg</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>1.65</drawSize>
          <color>(150,195,230)</color>
        </bodyGraphicData>
        <dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Warg/Dessicated_Warg</texPath>
          <drawSize>1.65</drawSize>
        </dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

  <!-- =================================================================
       RUT_VWake — the V-wake (propane lakes, submerged)
       ================================================================= -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RUT_VWake</defName>
    <label>v-wake</label>
    <description>You rarely see the thing itself — only the V-shaped ripple it cuts across the black mirror of the lake, closing fast. Propane-native from nose to tail, it hunts anything that disturbs the surface: a boot, a pipe, a hull. Crews running the pumps learn to read the wake before they learn much else about the lake.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>5.5</MoveSpeed>
      <Mass>28</Mass>
      <MarketValue>220</MarketValue>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>-100</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>-30</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <Wildness>0.95</Wildness>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>fangs</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>16</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.8</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Mouth</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>head</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>4</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>HeadAttackTool</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <ensureLinkedBodyPartsGroupAlwaysUsable>true</ensureLinkedBodyPartsGroupAlwaysUsable>
        <chanceFactor>0.2</chanceFactor>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <race>
      <!-- serpentine ambush shape, no limbs: fits "you rarely see the
           thing itself, only the wake." Vanilla Core BodyDef, zero new
           authoring. -->
      <body>Snake</body>
      <bloodDef>Filth_Blood</bloodDef>
      <bloodSmearDef>Filth_BloodSmear</bloodSmearDef>
      <baseBodySize>1.1</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>0.8</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.4</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>CarnivoreAnimal</foodType>
      <predator>true</predator>
      <maxPreyBodySize>1.2</maxPreyBodySize>
      <canBePredatorPrey>false</canBePredatorPrey>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <lifeExpectancy>12</lifeExpectancy>
      <!-- "attacking pawns and pipe on sight" (the_propane_lakes.md §4):
           standing in for the ruled pump-noise trigger until
           PROPANE_LAKE_PIPE_MECHANICS_1 lands (see file header). -->
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>1.0</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <manhunterOnTameFailChance>0.5</manhunterOnTameFailChance>
      <!-- the mechanism RSW_SandoAquaMonster already uses to live on an
           impassable water biome (SeaBeasts_Sando.xml, RUT_TheScald's own
           floor resident): treats liquid propane as passable, cost 1, for
           this race only. -->
      <waterSeeker>true</waterSeeker>
      <waterCellCost>1</waterCellCost>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.15</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.4</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
    </race>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.BlueDesert.RM_HydrocarbonNativeExtension" />
    </modExtensions>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalFighter</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RUT_VWake</defName>
    <label>v-wake</label>
    <race>RUT_VWake</race>
    <combatPower>80</combatPower>
    <wildGroupSize>1</wildGroupSize>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0.15</ecoSystemWeight>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RUT_VWake/RUT_VWake</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.9</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RUT_VWake/RUT_VWake</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>1.3</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RUT_VWake/RUT_VWake</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>1.7</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

</Defs>
